"Doug Freyburger" <dfreybur@yahoo.com> writes:
> Kevin Wayne wrote:
> >
> > Does in-game luck have an effect on the chances for gaining intrinsics?
> 
> No effect from character luck.
> 
> > I ask this because it's been my experience that I tend to gain
> > intrinsics much more successfully after I've gained the luckstone.
> >
> > Or maybe it's character level?
> 
> I would need to check to be certain but I think it's the
> monster's level not your character's level.  It's why
> dragons that can convey intrinsics always seem to.  The
> indirect link is higher character level allows higher
> level monsters.

To be more accurate, it's the monster type's _base_ level that
matters, not whatever the individual monster happened to be when it
died. Thus, draining a monster's level doesn't hurt your chance of
getting intrinsics out of it, nor does feeding it gain level potions
help.

